<div class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">BRING YOUR HISTORY</p><h1>Import your history</h1><p>Preview a Tiller workbook or transaction CSV before saving. No bank connection required.</p></div></div>
<section class="card padded content-narrow"><%= form_with url: imports_path, multipart: true, class: 'stack-form' do %>
<label>Reusable mapping <%= select_tag :profile_id, options_from_collection_for_select(@profiles, :id, :name), include_blank: 'Detect headers automatically' %></label>
<label>Tiller Excel workbook (up to 25 MB) or UTF-8 CSV (up to 5 MB) <%= file_field_tag :file, accept: '.xlsx,.csv,text/csv,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet', required: true %></label>
<div class="form-actions"><%= submit_tag 'Upload and preview', class: 'primary-button', data: { turbo_submits_with: 'Preparing preview…' } %></div><% end %>
<p class="import-help"><strong>Tiller:</strong> Upload the whole .xlsx workbook. Worth reads Transactions, Categories, Accounts and Balance History, converts amount signs automatically, and lets you match existing accounts. Historical balances come from Balance History; charts are rebuilt in Worth. CSV mappings do not apply to workbooks.</p>
<p class="import-help"><strong>CSV:</strong> Required columns: date, description, amount. Category and source account are optional. Dates: YYYY-MM-DD or MM/DD/YYYY. Positive amounts are spending; negative amounts are income. CSV imports leave balances unchanged.</p><p>No import creates bank connections. Review the preview and confirm to save your history.</p></section>
<% if @recent_imports.any? %>
<section class="card padded"><h2>Recent workbook imports</h2><p>Upload an updated workbook to add new records. Saved account matches and existing entries are kept.</p><ul><% @recent_imports.each do |batch| %><li><%= link_to batch.settings['source_filename'].presence || 'Tiller workbook', import_path(batch) %> · <%= batch.imported_at.to_date %><small><%= number_with_delimiter(batch.settings.dig('result', 'transactions').to_i) %> transactions added · <%= number_with_delimiter(batch.settings.dig('result', 'balances').to_i) %> daily balances added</small></li><% end %></ul></section>
<% end %>
